  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Shigin is the chanting of kanshi, poems in classical Chinese read in Japanese, and of Japanese verse, a practice that spread from late Edo-period academies and became a mass amateur art in the twentieth century through schools such as the Nihon Shigin Gakuin. It also accompanies kenshibu sword and fan dance, and Nippon Columbia and King issued many recordings.",
